[32m+ # Forge40 Coaching & Longevity Web Application[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ This repository contains the complete scaffolding and full high-converting landing page for **Forge40**—an AI-assisted strength and longevity coaching system designed for busy adults aged 40+ who want to build sustainable strength, prevent injury, and optimize their healthspan.[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ ## Directory Structure[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ ```[m
[32m+ /code[m
[32m+   ├── README.md             # This document[m
[32m+   ├── package.json          # Root orchestration package.json[m
[32m+   ├── frontend/             # Vite + React + Tailwind CSS v4 frontend[m
[32m+   │     ├── dist/           # Built static production-ready website assets[m
[32m+   │     ├── src/            # React source code components[m
[32m+   │     │     ├── App.jsx   # Beautiful, interactive responsive landing page[m
[32m+   │     │     ├── main.jsx  # Frontend entry point[m
[32m+   │     │     └── index.css # Tailwind directive import[m
[32m+   │     ├── index.html      # Main HTML layout[m
[32m+   │     └── vite.config.js  # Vite config using @tailwindcss/vite plugin[m
[32m+   └── backend/              # Express + Node.js + SQLite local backend[m
[32m+         ├── server.js       # Express server hosting port 3000, serving /frontend/dist[m
[32m+         ├── database.sqlite # Local SQLite database storage[m
[32m+         └── package.json    # Backend configuration & script definitions[m
[32m+ ```[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ ## Stack Details[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ 1. **Frontend:**[m
[32m+    - **Vite + React:** Extremely fast, lightweight, and memory-efficient frontend bundler.[m
[32m+    - **Tailwind CSS v4:** Modern CSS framework integrated natively into Vite using the new `@tailwindcss/vite` compiler plugin, requiring no config files and yielding incredibly tiny CSS bundles.[m
[32m+    - **Interactive State Features:**[m
[32m+      - *Interactive Assessment Teaser Quiz:* A 3-step physical scoring widget that drives users to complete their longevity analysis, prompting paid actions.[m
[32m+      - *Forge40 AI Coach Chat Demo:* A real-time conversational simulation showing off the unlimited AI chatbot included in the Membership tier.[m
[32m+      - *FAQ Accordion:* Expands and collapses top user objections to increase engagement.[m
[32m+      - *Pricing billing switcher:* Easily alternates between monthly ($29) and annual ($199) subscription terms with clear discount tracking.[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ 2. **Backend:**[m
[32m+    - **Node/Express:** Serve frontend static files from `/frontend/dist` and proxy all client routes securely.[m
[32m+    - **SQLite:** A local, fast, file-based database `/backend/database.sqlite` containing:[m
[32m+      - `newsletter_subscribers` - capturing high-intent email leads.[m
[32m+      - `assessment_completions` - records longevity markers and scores for analytics.[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ ## Getting Started[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ ### Prerequisites[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ - Node.js (v18 or higher)[m
[32m+ - npm (v9 or higher)[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ ### Installation & Build[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ 1. **Clone the repository:**[m
[32m+    ```bash[m
[32m+    git clone https://github.com/sacredsound/Forge40.git[m
[32m+    cd Forge40[m
[32m+    ```[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ 2. **Install frontend dependencies and build:**[m
[32m+    ```bash[m
[32m+    cd frontend[m
[32m+    npm install[m
[32m+    npm run build[m
[32m+    ```[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ 3. **Install backend dependencies:**[m
[32m+    ```bash[m
[32m+    cd ../backend[m
[32m+    npm install[m
[32m+    ```[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ ### Running the App[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ To run the web application in production mode:[m
[32m+ ```bash[m
[32m+ cd backend[m
[32m+ npm start[m
[32m+ ```[m
[32m+ The application will start listening on port `3000` bound to `0.0.0.0`, making it available publicly at the team's public URL![m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ For local background execution (to persist after exiting terminal):[m
[32m+ ```bash[m
[32m+ nohup npm start > /tmp/forge40-backend.log 2>&1 &[m
[32m+ ```[m
[32m+ You can view active connection states using:[m
[32m+ ```bash[m
[32m+ ss -Htln | grep :3000[m
[32m+ ```[m
[32m+ And check server console logs at `/tmp/forge40-backend.log`.[m
